  "question": "A particle executes SHM of amplitude $4$ cm. Its speed at the mean position is $12$ cm/s. Find its speed, in cm/s, when it is $2\\sqrt{3}$ cm from the mean position.",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [],
  "answer": "",
  "numerical_answer": "6",
  "tolerance": "0",
  "solution": "$\\omega = \\dfrac{12}{4} = 3$ rad/s.\n$$v = \\omega\\sqrt{A^2 - x^2} = 3\\sqrt{16 - 12} = 6\\ \\text{cm/s}$$",
